        "denialFound": "Yes. OCCRP, 31 Aug 2023, quoting an Adani representative: \"these allegations are not only baseless and unsubstantiated but are rehashed from Hindenburg's allegations… all the Adani Group's publicly listed entities are in compliance with all applicable laws including the regulation relating to public share holdings\" (recorded as c004). Ahli and Chang did not respond to OCCRP. Chang told the Guardian he knew nothing about secret purchases: \"We are a simple business.\" OCCRP, 17 Feb 2026: an Adani spokesperson said the alleged \"front men\" are \"public shareholders\", and in a Feb 2023 written statement to their bank Ahli and Chang denied wrongdoing. The SC in Vishal Tiwari v UoI (3 Jan 2024, para 40) said: \"reliance on newspaper articles or reports by third-party organizations to question a comprehensive investigation by a specialized regulator does not inspire confidence\" (c007, confirmed at https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188573380/). Sources: https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/documents-provide-fresh-insight-into-allegations-of-stock-manipulation-that-rocked-indias-powerful-adani-group ; https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/bank-documents-expose-scale-of-secret-investments-in-adani-group-by-adani-family-associates",
        "innocentReading": "Ahli and Chang are long-standing independent business associates who invested their own money in Adani stock because, in their words to their bank, they \"had personal and business relationships with the family and trusted their business acumen\". Excel's advisory role would then be ordinary fund advice rather than control. OCCRP itself says \"There is no evidence that Chang and Ahli's money for their Adani Group investments came from the Adani family. The source of the funds is unknown.\" Under this reading the holdings are public float and the 75% cap is not breached. It stays open until SEBI or a court decides whether the two acted in concert with the promoters.",
        "reason": "The source says what the claim says. The quoted text reads: \"In at least two cases — representing Adani stock holdings that at one point reached $430 million — the mysterious investors turn out to have widely reported ties to… the Adani family\"; \"At one point in March 2017, the value of the investments in Adani Group stock was $430 million\"; \"An agreement for Excel to provide advisory services to EIFF and EMRF was signed for Excel by Vinod Adani himself in 2011\". The date, actors, amount and funds all match, and the ₹ figure is a labelled approximation. The claim carries two contras (Adani's denial, and the SC's holding on evidentiary weight), and the central legal question, whether the two acted for the promoters, has not been decided. SEBI rejected the funds' settlement bids in Aug 2026, so the FPI strand is still open. 'alleged' is the right tier for the edge's thrust. 'reported' would fit only the bare holding facts, and the \"instructions\" element rests on a single unnamed source. Guardian and FT co-published from shared documents, so they are not independent outlets and do not lift the tier to documented. The claim survives on substance but needs structural fixes: the predicate and the node.",
